A choice forms a nominal tagged union.

Each value contains one declared variant.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Status ::
        Ready,
        Waiting,
        Failed | message String |,
    ;
]

### Variant forms

A unit variant has no payload:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Ready
]

A payload variant uses a record body:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Failed | message String |
]

### Contract

- The declaration form is `Name :: variants ;`.
- An inline declaration closes on the line containing its `::`. A multiline declaration closes with `;` alone on its own line.
- Nothing may follow the declaration's closer on its line.
- Choice and variant names use `PascalCase`.
- A choice must declare at least one variant.
- Variant names must be unique.
- A payload record must contain at least one field.
- Payload field names must be unique.
- Payload fields require explicit types.
- Payload fields are immutable.
- Payload fields do not support defaults.
- Mutable payload field declarations are invalid.
- Shorthand payload declarations such as `Failed String` are invalid.
- Constructor-style declarations such as `Failed(String)` are invalid.
- Recursive choice declarations are deferred.
- A choice has nominal identity. Matching variants and payload shapes do not make two choices interchangeable.

Declaration placement follows @../language-overview/#blocks-and-statements (Blocks and statements).

Payload fields have concrete declared types. Constructors check values against
those exact types and cannot infer a non-generic field type from later uses.
Generic choice parameters follow the bounded rules in
@../generics (Generics).

### Choice declaration MON data boundary

Nominal identity above is unchanged: matching variants and payload shapes never make two choices interchangeable. MON literal choice data follows the same declaration shapes by reference, with contextual `::Variant` or one exact `Choice::Variant` qualifier checked against the receiving schema. Contextual `::Variant` source construction is deferred, and choice payload defaults remain excluded. That contract is Rust-only serialised-data documentation. See @../mon/#mon-format (MON format).

### Generic choices

Choices may introduce declaration-site generic parameters.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Maybe type A ::
        Some | value A |,
        Missing,
    ;
]

Generic inference and instance restrictions are documented by
@../generics (Generics).
